{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02329",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.97,
      "end_seconds": 7.31,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Okay, doctor, we're all set in here. I'll give you the numbers when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.64,
      "end_seconds": 13.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Good, thank you. Welcome, tell me what's brought you in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.98,
      "end_seconds": 26.23,
      "duration_seconds": 11.25,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay. Doctor, it's night sweats. That's what we're worried about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.19,
      "end_seconds": 34.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.66,
      "end_seconds": 46.04,
      "duration_seconds": 10.38,
      "text": "Oh, um, probably about two weeks. Yeah. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.76,
      "end_seconds": 50.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.71,
      "end_seconds": 54.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "It happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.88,
      "end_seconds": 59.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "So, is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.97,
      "end_seconds": 69.04,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.67,
      "end_seconds": 74.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.09,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.06,
      "end_seconds": 81.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Severe, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.23,
      "end_seconds": 86.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.92,
      "end_seconds": 90.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "It usually comes with tiredness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.43,
      "end_seconds": 98.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 98.81,
      "end_seconds": 106.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.27,
      "text": "Erm, tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.47,
      "end_seconds": 125.2,
      "duration_seconds": 17.73,
      "text": "I was getting to that! Oh, as for small painful spots on my fingers, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.97,
      "end_seconds": 130.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.8,
      "end_seconds": 135.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "About a eight out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.15,
      "end_seconds": 139.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "How frequently does it come?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.76,
      "end_seconds": 146.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.73,
      "end_seconds": 154.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.07,
      "end_seconds": 158.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "I'd say all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.96,
      "end_seconds": 165.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Any a fever for two weeks as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.62,
      "end_seconds": 167.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Mm, uh, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 168.5,
      "end_seconds": 172.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Yes, that's right, that's how it was."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 172.69,
      "end_seconds": 185.79,
      "duration_seconds": 13.1,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 21, BP is 126 over 67, temperature 38.9, SpO2 97 percent on room air, pulse is 94 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.47,
      "end_seconds": 188.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.81,
      "end_seconds": 194.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Alright, over here please and I'll take a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.3,
      "end_seconds": 198.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.52,
      "end_seconds": 219.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "There is a new murmur, small splinter lines under the nails and a tender spot on the finger pad."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.67,
      "end_seconds": 229.57,
      "duration_seconds": 5.9,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Alright, did you get weight loss, chest pain or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.67,
      "end_seconds": 236.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "No weight loss, chest pain or cough, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.39,
      "end_seconds": 244.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.65,
      "end_seconds": 247.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Uh, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.88,
      "end_seconds": 255.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.85,
      "end_seconds": 271.51,
      "duration_seconds": 14.66,
      "text": "Mm, it's omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux. My family kept telling me to get it checked. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.98,
      "end_seconds": 272.72,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "Mm-hmm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.68,
      "end_seconds": 284.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.71,
      "text": "Gliclazide. I take it 80 milligrams, twice a day. Before this I was on lansoprazole; that's been stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.04,
      "end_seconds": 286.94,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "Any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.94,
      "end_seconds": 291.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.46,
      "end_seconds": 294.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.27,
      "end_seconds": 299.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.58,
      "end_seconds": 302.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.57,
      "end_seconds": 307.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.71,
      "end_seconds": 320.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.05,
      "end_seconds": 328.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Um, my brother has epilepsy. Erm, my mother had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.1,
      "end_seconds": 336.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.52,
      "end_seconds": 351.8,
      "duration_seconds": 13.28,
      "text": "Actually, uh, I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.84,
      "end_seconds": 357.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.51,
      "end_seconds": 366.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Acid reflux, for about ten years. Yes, diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.74,
      "end_seconds": 372.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Right, right. Alright, acid reflux, that matches what I have here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.95,
      "end_seconds": 401.79,
      "duration_seconds": 21.84,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like possible infective endocarditis. Another possibility is a viral illness. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had night sweats for about two weeks, severe, and no weight loss or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 402.88,
      "end_seconds": 403.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Correct."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 404.68,
      "end_seconds": 437.59,
      "duration_seconds": 32.91,
      "text": "Blood cultures is what I'd like next, for possible endocarditis. I think blood tests makes sense here, for prolonged fever. I think an echocardiogram makes sense here, for new murmur. You need admission today for blood cultures and a heart scan. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. We'll catch up straight away. How would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 439.63,
      "end_seconds": 444.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "So, I come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 445.1,
      "end_seconds": 451.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 452.43,
      "end_seconds": 454.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 457.61,
      "end_seconds": 458.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}